{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "How to Create a User Manual"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about user manuals."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Learning Outcome"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the operating systems, server operating systems and relevant information related with the user manual."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find two manuals of a same kind of product, for example a TV."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read and compare both manuals."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a chart showing the similarities and differences between both manuals."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find two manuals of a same kind of product."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read and compare them."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a chart showing the similarities and differences between the manuals."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modal Verbs for Speculating - Could"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p><strong><i>Modal verbs</i></strong> help us expressing different intentions when we talk; obligation, permission, possibility, ability, advice or prohibition.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>You can use <strong><i>could</i></strong> when you want to make guesses or speculate about a particular event, in this case, we call them <strong><i>modal verbs for speculating.</i></strong></p> <p>You can use the <strong><i>modal verbs of speculation</i></strong> followed by an infinitive to make guesses or express your opinion based on a fact.</p> <p>Structure:</p> <p>Affirmative: <strong>Subject + modal verb + verb (base form) + complement.</strong></p> <p>Negative: <strong>Subject + modal verb + not + verb (base form) + complement.</strong></p> <p>Interrogative: <strong>Modal verb + Subject + verb (base form) + complement + ?</strong></p> <p><i>Examples:</i></p> <ul> <li><i>To create individual pages designs, <strong>you&nbsp;</strong><strong>could keep </strong>in mind the colors and the font type you have been using in the other pages.</i></li> <li><i>I guess <strong>you couldn&rsquo;t&nbsp;</strong><strong>wait</strong> until the presentation to show us the new manual.</i></li> <li><strong><i>Could you tell if</i></strong><i> the manual we are about to implement is covering the current issue we have with the software privileges? </i></li> </ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Pictures and diagrams could be good visual aids to keep the style on the pages."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Creators could try to catch users' attention from the very first moment use big font size to highlight important aspects."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "How to Give Instructions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "From time to time you need to provide customers with a set of instructions to illustrate them on how to something. It is important you learn how to do it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "These are some tips you should take into account when giving instructions: </br> </br> <ul> 1.\tDon't assume your readers know the same you do. </br> 2.\tSet your goal clear, otherwise your manual will be either too long or too simple. </br> 3.\tCreate a draft, this will help you have a big picture of it will look. </br> 4.\tKeep it simple, use table of contents and graphics, they help users understanding. </br> 5.\tAsk someone to read it and give you feedback. </br> 6.\tKeep it short, do not overwhelm users with lots of information they may not need. </ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Pictures and diagrams could also be good visual aids to keep the style on the pages."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Creators could try to draw users' attention from the very beginning by implementing large-sized fonts to highlight important aspects."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "aim"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "goal or objective  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should also set your aim clear and let the user know your objective."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be proper or appropriate for something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The user manual should fit the size; if your product isn't too big, you should watch the proportions."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "patronize"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to act in an arrogant way "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You need to make it easy to understand too, avoiding patronizing and confusing font styles."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "set"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to establish or apply something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should also set your aim clear and let the user know your objective."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "visual aid"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an object used to illustrate or exemplify "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Pictures and diagrams could also be good visual aids to keep the style on the pages."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wrap up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to summarize or conclude"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let's wrap up what we've been studying lately."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob09aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n6le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<p><strong>Teacher</strong>: Let&rsquo;s wrap up what we&rsquo;ve been studying lately. If you want to design a user manual, how should one give instructions, and what should one bear in mind?</p>\n<p><strong>Noah</strong>: If you want to make sure your users get it right, you shouldn&rsquo;t assume they know the information you already know. You should also set your aim clear and let the user know your objective.</p>\n<p><strong>Ava</strong>: You need to make it easy to understand too, avoiding patronizing and confusing font styles.</p>\n<p><strong>Teacher</strong>: What about the design itself? The physical product?</p>"}, {"time": "32000", "image": "enpe8n6le02ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<p><strong>Noah</strong>: The user manual should fit the size; if your product isn&rsquo;t too big, you should watch the proportions.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Ava</strong>: It is important you also consider the type of paper you use for the manual; it could be something resistant and eye-catching. Try not to overwhelm the user with lots of information they might feel useless. Pictures and diagrams could also be good visual aids to keep the style on the pages.</p>\n<p><strong>Noah</strong>: Creators could try to draw users&rsquo; attention from the very beginning by implementing large-sized fonts to highlight important aspects. I believe most users don&rsquo;t get to read the manuals, only if they must; thus, it could be a good opportunity to connect better with customers.</p>"}, {"time": "80000", "image": "enpe8n6le02ob09re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<p><strong>Teacher</strong>: What are some other aspects to consider when creating the hardcopy of the manual?</p>\n<p><strong>Ava</strong>: You should provide enough space between sections to avoid confusion and use color coding if necessary. You should also consider where the manual will be used, and if it needs to be resistant to water, oil, or dirt.</p>\n<p><strong>Noah</strong>: Users will probably prefer durable covers and pages to make sure the manual can lie flat when it is open.</p>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n6le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe8n6le02ob09re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain how to give instructions and how to design individual pages in the user manual."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe how to create a physical manual."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What information do you think should be written in manuals?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you think manuals should look like? Why?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, 